Sun Oct 18 05:59:52 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 2.2:
  - Robustness release, upgrade is recommended when processing BIE
    or PBM/PGM data from untrusted sources.
  - The jbig.c decoder now caps the final image layer at 2 GB by
    default via the new sd->maxmem limit (adjustable), mitigating
    denial of service through excessive image dimensions.
  - pbmtojbg and pbmtojbg85 validate PBM/PGM header dimensions and
    check size calculations against integer overflow.
  - Fixed jbg85_dec_finalheight() macro typo, a jbg_enc_options()
    range check, jbgtopbm division by zero, and several converter
    file-handling fixes.
  - struct jbg_dec_state gained maxmem: libjbig consumers must be
    recompiled against the new headers (soname unchanged).
  - Dropped jbigkit-CVE-2022-1210.patch, superseded upstream;
    rebased jbigkit-2.1-shlib.patch to the 2.2 sources, fixing
    parallel-build races in the test programs and test suite.
- Spec cleanup: BuildRequires for gcc and make,
  %ldconfig_scriptlets, https source URL.

